{"type":"text","timestamp":1788182960606,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","part":{"id":"prt_05802981c001hzqAbDHzYdsA2u","messageID":"msg_058026d47001wfhQJUXsYj3PCh","sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","type":"text","text":"Writing the five output files now. I’m keeping the JSON and CSV evidence anchored to specific modules and functions so they can be checked mechanically.","time":{"start":1788182960156,"end":1788182960598},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_03d5adaf75aabf8c016a9581b0122487d29c67435d63e7cc45","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183061031,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_bDopY9aJImFxjgGultZjYCyO","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/module_map.json\n+{\n+  \"modules\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/cli.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"CLI bootstrap that loads settings, initializes the SQLite schema, and prints readiness information.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.config\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/config.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Configuration model and environment-based settings loader for database path and readonly mode.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/models.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Defines the in-memory Order dataclass shared by handlers, audit logic, and persistence.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/audit.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Builds ephemeral order event payloads returned to callers; it does not persist them.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Implements create and read order use cases for the HTTP adapter layer.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Registers HTTP route callbacks that delegate to handler functions.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/storage/repo.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"SQLite-backed repository for schema creation, order inserts, and order lookups.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"entry_points\": [\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"kind\": \"cli\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"pyproject.toml [project.scripts].minisvc\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"kind\": \"http_route_registration\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"called by an external web app object with post/get methods\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"kind\": \"request_handler\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"registered by minisvc.api.routes:register_routes for POST /orders\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"kind\": \"request_handler\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"registered by minisvc.api.routes:register_routes for GET /orders/<order_id>\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"dependency_edges\": [\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.config\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"environment.MINISVC_DB, environment.MINISVC_READONLY\",\n+      \"type\": \"reads_config\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\",\n+      \"type\": \"instantiates\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models:Order\",\n+      \"type\": \"instantiates\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"key_functions\": [\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Primary executable entry point. Loads env settings, opens the repository against the configured SQLite path, initializes the orders table, and returns exit code 0.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Parses no CLI arguments even though argv is accepted.\",\n+        \"Loads readonly configuration but does not enforce it.\",\n+        \"Creates schema on startup as a side effect.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Converts environment variables into a frozen Settings object.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Defaults database_path to orders.sqlite.\",\n+        \"Treats MINISVC_READONLY=1 as true and everything else as false.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Binds POST and GET order endpoints onto an external app object using lambdas that capture the repository.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Assumes the app exposes post and get registration methods.\",\n+        \"Does not own app construction or server startup.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Builds an Order from request payload fields, persists it, and returns a created response with an audit-style event payload.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Requires payload keys order_id, customer, and total_cents.\",\n+        \"Casts total_cents with int().\",\n+        \"Does not catch validation or database exceptions.\",\n+        \"Does not retry failed writes or consult readonly settings.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Fetches an order by id and returns either a missing response or the order contents plus an audit-style read event.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Returns order.__dict__ directly for successful reads.\",\n+        \"No explicit input validation beyond repository query parameterization.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Constructs a dictionary describing an order action for API responses.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Pure function with no storage or external side effects.\",\n+        \"Supports both created and read actions based on caller input.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Ensures the orders table exists in SQLite.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Only creates the orders table; there is no audit table.\",\n+        \"Relies on sqlite3 context manager transaction behavior.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Inserts an Order into the orders table.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Opens a new SQLite connection per call.\",\n+        \"No retry loop, upsert behavior, or error handling.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Looks up an order row by primary key and reconstructs an Order object if found.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Uses a parameterized query for order_id.\",\n+        \"Returns None when no row exists.\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"runtime_flows\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"CLI startup flow\",\n+      \"steps\": [\n+        \"The packaging script entry point invokes minisvc.cli:main.\",\n+        \"main reads process environment and calls minisvc.config:load_settings.\",\n+        \"load_settings builds Settings with database_path and readonly fields.\",\n+        \"main instantiates minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository using settings.database_path.\",\n+        \"main calls OrderRepository.init_schema, which creates the SQLite orders table if needed.\",\n+        \"main prints a readiness message containing the database path and exits with status code 0.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"HTTP create-order flow\",\n+      \"steps\": [\n+        \"An external web app calls minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo).\",\n+        \"register_routes binds POST /orders to a lambda that forwards payload and repo into minisvc.api.handlers:create_order.\",\n+        \"create_order reads payload['order_id'], payload['customer'], and payload['total_cents'] and constructs minisvc.models:Order.\",\n+        \"create_order calls OrderRepository.save, which inserts the record into the SQLite orders table.\",\n+        \"create_order calls minisvc.audit:order_event with action='created'.\",\n+        \"create_order returns a response dict containing status, order_id, and the generated event payload.\",\n+        \"If payload fields are missing or SQLite insert fails, the exception propagates because no handler catches it.\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/architecture.md\n+# minisvc Architecture Summary\n+\n+## What This Service Actually Contains\n+\n+`minisvc` is a very small Python service skeleton with two real runtime surfaces:\n+\n+- A CLI bootstrap entry point at `minisvc.cli:main`\n+- An HTTP route registration hook at `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n+\n+It persists orders to a local SQLite database through `OrderRepository`. The package marker files `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` do not contain business logic, and `minisvc/__init__.py` only exports names.\n+\n+## Runtime Modules\n+\n+- `minisvc/cli.py`: startup path for the packaged `minisvc` command. Loads config, opens the repository, creates schema, prints readiness.\n+- `minisvc/config.py`: defines `Settings` and `load_settings(env)`, reading `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY`.\n+- `minisvc/models.py`: defines the `Order` dataclass.\n+- `minisvc/audit.py`: builds an event dictionary for API responses. It does not write any audit records.\n+- `minisvc/api/routes.py`: attaches HTTP handlers to an external app object via `app.post(...)` and `app.get(...)`.\n+- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`: implements create and read order actions.\n+- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`: owns SQLite schema creation and CRUD-like persistence for orders.\n+\n+## Entry Points\n+\n+- `minisvc.cli:main`: declared in `pyproject.toml` as the `minisvc` console script.\n+- `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`: integration point for wiring HTTP routes into a framework-specific app.\n+- `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order`: POST `/orders` behavior after route registration.\n+- `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order`: GET `/orders/<order_id>` behavior after route registration.\n+\n+## Data Flow\n+\n+### CLI startup\n+\n+1. `minisvc.cli:main` reads process environment.\n+2. `minisvc.config:load_settings` builds a `Settings` object.\n+3. `main` creates `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n+4. `OrderRepository.init_schema()` creates the `orders` table if it is missing.\n+5. The CLI prints `minisvc ready at ...` and exits.\n+\n+### HTTP create-order flow\n+\n+1. Some external application constructs a repository and calls `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo)`.\n+2. The registered POST callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order(payload, repo)`.\n+3. `create_order` extracts `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` from the payload and builds an `Order` dataclass.\n+4. `repo.save(order)` inserts the order into SQLite.\n+5. `order_event(order, \"created\")` generates a response event object.\n+6. The handler returns a dictionary response.\n+\n+### HTTP read flow\n+\n+1. The registered GET callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n+2. `repo.get(order_id)` reads a row from SQLite.\n+3. The handler returns either `{\"status\": \"missing\"}` or `{\"status\": \"ok\", \"order\": ..., \"event\": ...}`.\n+\n+## Storage\n+\n+- Storage engine: SQLite via Python `sqlite3`\n+- Path source: `MINISVC_DB`, defaulting to `orders.sqlite`\n+- Schema ownership: `OrderRepository.init_schema()`\n+- Tables actually created: only `orders`\n+- Audit persistence: none\n+\n+Each repository method opens a fresh SQLite connection with `sqlite3.connect(self.database_path)`. There is no connection pooling, no retry wrapper, and no migration/versioning layer.\n+\n+## Documentation vs Code Reality\n+\n+The README explicitly says the code is authoritative when docs disagree. In practice, the implementation is simpler than the design notes:\n+\n+- `MINISVC_READONLY=1` is parsed into `Settings.readonly`, but no write path checks it.\n+- `create_order` does not retry failed SQLite writes.\n+- Audit events are returned in response payloads only; there is no durable audit table.\n+\n+## Risks And Extension Points\n+\n+### Risks\n+\n+- Error handling is minimal. Missing payload keys, bad integer conversion, duplicate primary keys, or SQLite failures will raise exceptions directly from handlers.\n+- Configuration is only partly wired. `readonly` is loaded but ignored by the repository and handlers.\n+- Audit behavior is non-durable despite documentation claiming durable storage.\n+- The HTTP layer assumes an app object with `.post` and `.get`, but the repository contains no app factory or server bootstrap, so runtime integration is external and implicit.\n+\n+### Extension points\n+\n+- Enforce readonly mode in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` or inside `OrderRepository.save`.\n+- Add explicit request validation and translate failures into stable API responses.\n+- Introduce durable audit persistence in `minisvc/storage/repo.py` or a separate audit repository.\n+- Add an application bootstrap module that constructs the app and calls `register_routes` to make the HTTP runtime self-contained.\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\n+claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n+\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads readonly into Settings; minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) unconditionally; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs insert with no readonly check\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may assume writes are prevented in readonly mode and accidentally modify production or maintenance databases.\"\n+\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 contains a single repo.save(order) call; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs one insert and has no retry loop or exception handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures will surface immediately and may produce unhandled 500-style failures instead of controlled retry behavior.\"\n+\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only builds a dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table; no module writes audit records\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may rely on an audit trail that does not exist, weakening compliance, debugging, and incident reconstruction.\"\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/risk_register.csv\n+risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\n+R1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 inserts directly into a local SQLite file; each method opens a new connection and there is no backup, migration, or retry layer\",\"Order data durability depends on a single local file and can be fragile in ephemeral or poorly managed runtime environments\",\"Define supported deployment storage, add backup/migration guidance, and consider a managed DB or explicit durability procedures\",\"Platform plus service owner\"\n+R2,audit behavior,\"README.md:8 claims durable audit storage, but minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an event dict and minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for created or read actions, limiting compliance evidence and post-incident analysis\",\"Either implement persisted audit records or remove/replace the claim and document the current ephemeral behavior\",\"Service owner\"\n+R3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY; minisvc/cli.py:8-11 uses database_path but no runtime code consults Settings.readonly\",\"Runtime behavior does not match configuration expectations, and defaulting to orders.sqlite may place data in an unintended working directory\",\"Enforce readonly mode in write paths and document or validate the database file location at startup\",\"Service owner\"\n+R4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 accesses payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(); no try/except or schema validation is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError and bubble up as unstable API failures\",\"Add request schema validation and convert validation failures into explicit client-facing error responses\",\"API owner\"\n+R5,HTTP integration contract,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes app.post and app.get methods, but the repo contains no app factory or framework dependency\",\"Integration can break silently if the host app contract differs, and new engineers have no in-repo runnable HTTP bootstrap\",\"Add a documented adapter contract or a concrete app bootstrap module with a smoke test\",\"Service owner\"\n*** Add File: /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md\n+# minisvc Onboarding Plan\n+\n+## Read Order\n+\n+1. `README.md` to learn the intended behavior and note that code is authoritative.\n+2. `pyproject.toml` to find the packaged CLI entry point.\n+3. `minisvc/cli.py` for the simplest real runtime path.\n+4. `minisvc/config.py` and `minisvc/storage/repo.py` for configuration and persistence.\n+5. `minisvc/api/routes.py` and `minisvc/api/handlers.py` for request flow.\n+6. `minisvc/models.py` and `minisvc/audit.py` for shared data structures.\n+\n+Active runtime code is in the modules above. `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package markers, and `minisvc/__init__.py` is a minimal export file rather than business logic.\n+\n+## Local Run And Test Commands\n+\n+Run from the repository root:\n+\n+```bash\n+python -m minisvc.cli\n+MINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python -m minisvc.cli\n+python -m compileall minisvc\n+```\n+\n+There is no in-repo HTTP server bootstrap or automated test suite. For a quick handler smoke test:\n+\n+```bash\n+python - <<'PY'\n+from minisvc.api.handlers import create_order\n+from minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\n+\n+repo = OrderRepository('/tmp/minisvc-smoke.sqlite')\n+repo.init_schema()\n+print(create_order({'order_id': 'o-1', 'customer': 'Taylor', 'total_cents': '1234'}, repo))\n+PY\n+```\n+\n+## First Breakpoint Or Trace Point\n+\n+Start at `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order` on the `repo.save(order)` line.\n+\n+Why this spot:\n+\n+- It sits on the main write path.\n+- You can inspect payload parsing, `Order` construction, and the transition into SQLite persistence.\n+- It quickly reveals that readonly mode and retry behavior are not enforced.\n+\n+## Two Safe First Changes\n+\n+1. Add explicit request validation in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` so missing fields and bad `total_cents` values return stable errors instead of raw exceptions.\n+2. Wire `Settings.readonly` into the write path, either by checking it before `repo.save(order)` or by enforcing it in `OrderRepository.save`.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/module_map.json\nA workspace/out/architecture.md\nA workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\nA workspace/out/risk_register.csv\nA workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/out/module_map.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/module_map.json\n+++ /workspace/out/module_map.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,275 @@\n+{\n+  \"modules\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/cli.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"CLI bootstrap that loads settings, initializes the SQLite schema, and prints readiness information.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.config\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/config.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Configuration model and environment-based settings loader for database path and readonly mode.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/models.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Defines the in-memory Order dataclass shared by handlers, audit logic, and persistence.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/audit.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Builds ephemeral order event payloads returned to callers; it does not persist them.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Implements create and read order use cases for the HTTP adapter layer.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Registers HTTP route callbacks that delegate to handler functions.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/storage/repo.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"SQLite-backed repository for schema creation, order inserts, and order lookups.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"entry_points\": [\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"kind\": \"cli\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"pyproject.toml [project.scripts].minisvc\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"kind\": \"http_route_registration\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"called by an external web app object with post/get methods\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"kind\": \"request_handler\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"registered by minisvc.api.routes:register_routes for POST /orders\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"kind\": \"request_handler\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"registered by minisvc.api.routes:register_routes for GET /orders/<order_id>\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"dependency_edges\": [\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.config\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"environment.MINISVC_DB, environment.MINISVC_READONLY\",\n+      \"type\": \"reads_config\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\",\n+      \"type\": \"instantiates\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models:Order\",\n+      \"type\": \"instantiates\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"key_functions\": [\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Primary executable entry point. Loads env settings, opens the repository against the configured SQLite path, initializes the orders table, and returns exit code 0.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Parses no CLI arguments even though argv is accepted.\",\n+        \"Loads readonly configuration but does not enforce it.\",\n+        \"Creates schema on startup as a side effect.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Converts environment variables into a frozen Settings object.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Defaults database_path to orders.sqlite.\",\n+        \"Treats MINISVC_READONLY=1 as true and everything else as false.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Binds POST and GET order endpoints onto an external app object using lambdas that capture the repository.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Assumes the app exposes post and get registration methods.\",\n+        \"Does not own app construction or server startup.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Builds an Order from request payload fields, persists it, and returns a created response with an audit-style event payload.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Requires payload keys order_id, customer, and total_cents.\",\n+        \"Casts total_cents with int().\",\n+        \"Does not catch validation or database exceptions.\",\n+        \"Does not retry failed writes or consult readonly settings.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Fetches an order by id and returns either a missing response or the order contents plus an audit-style read event.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Returns order.__dict__ directly for successful reads.\",\n+        \"No explicit input validation beyond repository query parameterization.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Constructs a dictionary describing an order action for API responses.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Pure function with no storage or external side effects.\",\n+        \"Supports both created and read actions based on caller input.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Ensures the orders table exists in SQLite.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Only creates the orders table; there is no audit table.\",\n+        \"Relies on sqlite3 context manager transaction behavior.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Inserts an Order into the orders table.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Opens a new SQLite connection per call.\",\n+        \"No retry loop, upsert behavior, or error handling.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Looks up an order row by primary key and reconstructs an Order object if found.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Uses a parameterized query for order_id.\",\n+        \"Returns None when no row exists.\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"runtime_flows\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"CLI startup flow\",\n+      \"steps\": [\n+        \"The packaging script entry point invokes minisvc.cli:main.\",\n+        \"main reads process environment and calls minisvc.config:load_settings.\",\n+        \"load_settings builds Settings with database_path and readonly fields.\",\n+        \"main instantiates minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository using settings.database_path.\",\n+        \"main calls OrderRepository.init_schema, which creates the SQLite orders table if needed.\",\n+        \"main prints a readiness message containing the database path and exits with status code 0.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"HTTP create-order flow\",\n+      \"steps\": [\n+        \"An external web app calls minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo).\",\n+        \"register_routes binds POST /orders to a lambda that forwards payload and repo into minisvc.api.handlers:create_order.\",\n+        \"create_order reads payload['order_id'], payload['customer'], and payload['total_cents'] and constructs minisvc.models:Order.\",\n+        \"create_order calls OrderRepository.save, which inserts the record into the SQLite orders table.\",\n+        \"create_order calls minisvc.audit:order_event with action='created'.\",\n+        \"create_order returns a response dict containing status, order_id, and the generated event payload.\",\n+        \"If payload fields are missing or SQLite insert fails, the exception propagates because no handler catches it.\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n\nIndex: /workspace/out/architecture.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/architecture.md\n+++ /workspace/out/architecture.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@\n+# minisvc Architecture Summary\n+\n+## What This Service Actually Contains\n+\n+`minisvc` is a very small Python service skeleton with two real runtime surfaces:\n+\n+- A CLI bootstrap entry point at `minisvc.cli:main`\n+- An HTTP route registration hook at `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n+\n+It persists orders to a local SQLite database through `OrderRepository`. The package marker files `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` do not contain business logic, and `minisvc/__init__.py` only exports names.\n+\n+## Runtime Modules\n+\n+- `minisvc/cli.py`: startup path for the packaged `minisvc` command. Loads config, opens the repository, creates schema, prints readiness.\n+- `minisvc/config.py`: defines `Settings` and `load_settings(env)`, reading `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY`.\n+- `minisvc/models.py`: defines the `Order` dataclass.\n+- `minisvc/audit.py`: builds an event dictionary for API responses. It does not write any audit records.\n+- `minisvc/api/routes.py`: attaches HTTP handlers to an external app object via `app.post(...)` and `app.get(...)`.\n+- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`: implements create and read order actions.\n+- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`: owns SQLite schema creation and CRUD-like persistence for orders.\n+\n+## Entry Points\n+\n+- `minisvc.cli:main`: declared in `pyproject.toml` as the `minisvc` console script.\n+- `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`: integration point for wiring HTTP routes into a framework-specific app.\n+- `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order`: POST `/orders` behavior after route registration.\n+- `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order`: GET `/orders/<order_id>` behavior after route registration.\n+\n+## Data Flow\n+\n+### CLI startup\n+\n+1. `minisvc.cli:main` reads process environment.\n+2. `minisvc.config:load_settings` builds a `Settings` object.\n+3. `main` creates `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n+4. `OrderRepository.init_schema()` creates the `orders` table if it is missing.\n+5. The CLI prints `minisvc ready at ...` and exits.\n+\n+### HTTP create-order flow\n+\n+1. Some external application constructs a repository and calls `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo)`.\n+2. The registered POST callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order(payload, repo)`.\n+3. `create_order` extracts `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` from the payload and builds an `Order` dataclass.\n+4. `repo.save(order)` inserts the order into SQLite.\n+5. `order_event(order, \"created\")` generates a response event object.\n+6. The handler returns a dictionary response.\n+\n+### HTTP read flow\n+\n+1. The registered GET callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n+2. `repo.get(order_id)` reads a row from SQLite.\n+3. The handler returns either `{\"status\": \"missing\"}` or `{\"status\": \"ok\", \"order\": ..., \"event\": ...}`.\n+\n+## Storage\n+\n+- Storage engine: SQLite via Python `sqlite3`\n+- Path source: `MINISVC_DB`, defaulting to `orders.sqlite`\n+- Schema ownership: `OrderRepository.init_schema()`\n+- Tables actually created: only `orders`\n+- Audit persistence: none\n+\n+Each repository method opens a fresh SQLite connection with `sqlite3.connect(self.database_path)`. There is no connection pooling, no retry wrapper, and no migration/versioning layer.\n+\n+## Documentation vs Code Reality\n+\n+The README explicitly says the code is authoritative when docs disagree. In practice, the implementation is simpler than the design notes:\n+\n+- `MINISVC_READONLY=1` is parsed into `Settings.readonly`, but no write path checks it.\n+- `create_order` does not retry failed SQLite writes.\n+- Audit events are returned in response payloads only; there is no durable audit table.\n+\n+## Risks And Extension Points\n+\n+### Risks\n+\n+- Error handling is minimal. Missing payload keys, bad integer conversion, duplicate primary keys, or SQLite failures will raise exceptions directly from handlers.\n+- Configuration is only partly wired. `readonly` is loaded but ignored by the repository and handlers.\n+- Audit behavior is non-durable despite documentation claiming durable storage.\n+- The HTTP layer assumes an app object with `.post` and `.get`, but the repository contains no app factory or server bootstrap, so runtime integration is external and implicit.\n+\n+### Extension points\n+\n+- Enforce readonly mode in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` or inside `OrderRepository.save`.\n+- Add explicit request validation and translate failures into stable API responses.\n+- Introduce durable audit persistence in `minisvc/storage/repo.py` or a separate audit repository.\n+- Add an application bootstrap module that constructs the app and calls `register_routes` to make the HTTP runtime self-contained.\n\nIndex: /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\n+++ /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n+\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads readonly into Settings; minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) unconditionally; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs insert with no readonly check\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may assume writes are prevented in readonly mode and accidentally modify production or maintenance databases.\"\n+\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 contains a single repo.save(order) call; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs one insert and has no retry loop or exception handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures will surface immediately and may produce unhandled 500-style failures instead of controlled retry behavior.\"\n+\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only builds a dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table; no module writes audit records\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may rely on an audit trail that does not exist, weakening compliance, debugging, and incident reconstruction.\"\n\nIndex: /workspace/out/risk_register.csv\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/risk_register.csv\n+++ /workspace/out/risk_register.csv\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\n+R1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 inserts directly into a local SQLite file; each method opens a new connection and there is no backup, migration, or retry layer\",\"Order data durability depends on a single local file and can be fragile in ephemeral or poorly managed runtime environments\",\"Define supported deployment storage, add backup/migration guidance, and consider a managed DB or explicit durability procedures\",\"Platform plus service owner\"\n+R2,audit behavior,\"README.md:8 claims durable audit storage, but minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an event dict and minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for created or read actions, limiting compliance evidence and post-incident analysis\",\"Either implement persisted audit records or remove/replace the claim and document the current ephemeral behavior\",\"Service owner\"\n+R3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY; minisvc/cli.py:8-11 uses database_path but no runtime code consults Settings.readonly\",\"Runtime behavior does not match configuration expectations, and defaulting to orders.sqlite may place data in an unintended working directory\",\"Enforce readonly mode in write paths and document or validate the database file location at startup\",\"Service owner\"\n+R4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 accesses payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(); no try/except or schema validation is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError and bubble up as unstable API failures\",\"Add request schema validation and convert validation failures into explicit client-facing error responses\",\"API owner\"\n+R5,HTTP integration contract,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes app.post and app.get methods, but the repo contains no app factory or framework dependency\",\"Integration can break silently if the host app contract differs, and new engineers have no in-repo runnable HTTP bootstrap\",\"Add a documented adapter contract or a concrete app bootstrap module with a smoke test\",\"Service owner\"\n\nIndex: /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md\n+++ /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@\n+# minisvc Onboarding Plan\n+\n+## Read Order\n+\n+1. `README.md` to learn the intended behavior and note that code is authoritative.\n+2. `pyproject.toml` to find the packaged CLI entry point.\n+3. `minisvc/cli.py` for the simplest real runtime path.\n+4. `minisvc/config.py` and `minisvc/storage/repo.py` for configuration and persistence.\n+5. `minisvc/api/routes.py` and `minisvc/api/handlers.py` for request flow.\n+6. `minisvc/models.py` and `minisvc/audit.py` for shared data structures.\n+\n+Active runtime code is in the modules above. `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package markers, and `minisvc/__init__.py` is a minimal export file rather than business logic.\n+\n+## Local Run And Test Commands\n+\n+Run from the repository root:\n+\n+```bash\n+python -m minisvc.cli\n+MINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python -m minisvc.cli\n+python -m compileall minisvc\n+```\n+\n+There is no in-repo HTTP server bootstrap or automated test suite. For a quick handler smoke test:\n+\n+```bash\n+python - <<'PY'\n+from minisvc.api.handlers import create_order\n+from minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\n+\n+repo = OrderRepository('/tmp/minisvc-smoke.sqlite')\n+repo.init_schema()\n+print(create_order({'order_id': 'o-1', 'customer': 'Taylor', 'total_cents': '1234'}, repo))\n+PY\n+```\n+\n+## First Breakpoint Or Trace Point\n+\n+Start at `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order` on the `repo.save(order)` line.\n+\n+Why this spot:\n+\n+- It sits on the main write path.\n+- You can inspect payload parsing, `Order` construction, and the transition into SQLite persistence.\n+- It quickly reveals that readonly mode and retry behavior are not enforced.\n+\n+## Two Safe First Changes\n+\n+1. Add explicit request validation in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` so missing fields and bad `total_cents` values return stable errors instead of raw exceptions.\n+2. Wire `Settings.readonly` into the write path, either by checking it before `repo.save(order)` or by enforcing it in `OrderRepository.save`.\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/out/module_map.json","relativePath":"workspace/out/module_map.json","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/module_map.json\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/module_map.json\n+++ /workspace/out/module_map.json\n@@ -0,0 +1,275 @@\n+{\n+  \"modules\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/cli.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"CLI bootstrap that loads settings, initializes the SQLite schema, and prints readiness information.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.config\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/config.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Configuration model and environment-based settings loader for database path and readonly mode.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/models.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Defines the in-memory Order dataclass shared by handlers, audit logic, and persistence.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/audit.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Builds ephemeral order event payloads returned to callers; it does not persist them.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/handlers.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Implements create and read order use cases for the HTTP adapter layer.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/api/routes.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"Registers HTTP route callbacks that delegate to handler functions.\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"path\": \"minisvc/storage/repo.py\",\n+      \"purpose\": \"SQLite-backed repository for schema creation, order inserts, and order lookups.\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"entry_points\": [\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"kind\": \"cli\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"pyproject.toml [project.scripts].minisvc\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"kind\": \"http_route_registration\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"called by an external web app object with post/get methods\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"kind\": \"request_handler\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"registered by minisvc.api.routes:register_routes for POST /orders\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"kind\": \"request_handler\",\n+      \"exposed_via\": \"registered by minisvc.api.routes:register_routes for GET /orders/<order_id>\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"dependency_edges\": [\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.config\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"environment.MINISVC_DB, environment.MINISVC_READONLY\",\n+      \"type\": \"reads_config\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository\",\n+      \"type\": \"instantiates\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models:Order\",\n+      \"type\": \"instantiates\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo\",\n+      \"to\": \"minisvc.models\",\n+      \"type\": \"imports\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"persists_to\"\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"from\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"to\": \"sqlite.orders\",\n+      \"type\": \"calls\"\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"key_functions\": [\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.cli:main\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Primary executable entry point. Loads env settings, opens the repository against the configured SQLite path, initializes the orders table, and returns exit code 0.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Parses no CLI arguments even though argv is accepted.\",\n+        \"Loads readonly configuration but does not enforce it.\",\n+        \"Creates schema on startup as a side effect.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.config:load_settings\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Converts environment variables into a frozen Settings object.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Defaults database_path to orders.sqlite.\",\n+        \"Treats MINISVC_READONLY=1 as true and everything else as false.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.routes:register_routes\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Binds POST and GET order endpoints onto an external app object using lambdas that capture the repository.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Assumes the app exposes post and get registration methods.\",\n+        \"Does not own app construction or server startup.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:create_order\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Builds an Order from request payload fields, persists it, and returns a created response with an audit-style event payload.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Requires payload keys order_id, customer, and total_cents.\",\n+        \"Casts total_cents with int().\",\n+        \"Does not catch validation or database exceptions.\",\n+        \"Does not retry failed writes or consult readonly settings.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Fetches an order by id and returns either a missing response or the order contents plus an audit-style read event.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Returns order.__dict__ directly for successful reads.\",\n+        \"No explicit input validation beyond repository query parameterization.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Constructs a dictionary describing an order action for API responses.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Pure function with no storage or external side effects.\",\n+        \"Supports both created and read actions based on caller input.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Ensures the orders table exists in SQLite.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Only creates the orders table; there is no audit table.\",\n+        \"Relies on sqlite3 context manager transaction behavior.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Inserts an Order into the orders table.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Opens a new SQLite connection per call.\",\n+        \"No retry loop, upsert behavior, or error handling.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n+      \"summary\": \"Looks up an order row by primary key and reconstructs an Order object if found.\",\n+      \"notable_details\": [\n+        \"Uses a parameterized query for order_id.\",\n+        \"Returns None when no row exists.\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ],\n+  \"runtime_flows\": [\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"CLI startup flow\",\n+      \"steps\": [\n+        \"The packaging script entry point invokes minisvc.cli:main.\",\n+        \"main reads process environment and calls minisvc.config:load_settings.\",\n+        \"load_settings builds Settings with database_path and readonly fields.\",\n+        \"main instantiates minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository using settings.database_path.\",\n+        \"main calls OrderRepository.init_schema, which creates the SQLite orders table if needed.\",\n+        \"main prints a readiness message containing the database path and exits with status code 0.\"\n+      ]\n+    },\n+    {\n+      \"name\": \"HTTP create-order flow\",\n+      \"steps\": [\n+        \"An external web app calls minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo).\",\n+        \"register_routes binds POST /orders to a lambda that forwards payload and repo into minisvc.api.handlers:create_order.\",\n+        \"create_order reads payload['order_id'], payload['customer'], and payload['total_cents'] and constructs minisvc.models:Order.\",\n+        \"create_order calls OrderRepository.save, which inserts the record into the SQLite orders table.\",\n+        \"create_order calls minisvc.audit:order_event with action='created'.\",\n+        \"create_order returns a response dict containing status, order_id, and the generated event payload.\",\n+        \"If payload fields are missing or SQLite insert fails, the exception propagates because no handler catches it.\"\n+      ]\n+    }\n+  ]\n+}\n","additions":275,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/out/architecture.md","relativePath":"workspace/out/architecture.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/architecture.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/architecture.md\n+++ /workspace/out/architecture.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,86 @@\n+# minisvc Architecture Summary\n+\n+## What This Service Actually Contains\n+\n+`minisvc` is a very small Python service skeleton with two real runtime surfaces:\n+\n+- A CLI bootstrap entry point at `minisvc.cli:main`\n+- An HTTP route registration hook at `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n+\n+It persists orders to a local SQLite database through `OrderRepository`. The package marker files `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` do not contain business logic, and `minisvc/__init__.py` only exports names.\n+\n+## Runtime Modules\n+\n+- `minisvc/cli.py`: startup path for the packaged `minisvc` command. Loads config, opens the repository, creates schema, prints readiness.\n+- `minisvc/config.py`: defines `Settings` and `load_settings(env)`, reading `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY`.\n+- `minisvc/models.py`: defines the `Order` dataclass.\n+- `minisvc/audit.py`: builds an event dictionary for API responses. It does not write any audit records.\n+- `minisvc/api/routes.py`: attaches HTTP handlers to an external app object via `app.post(...)` and `app.get(...)`.\n+- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`: implements create and read order actions.\n+- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`: owns SQLite schema creation and CRUD-like persistence for orders.\n+\n+## Entry Points\n+\n+- `minisvc.cli:main`: declared in `pyproject.toml` as the `minisvc` console script.\n+- `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`: integration point for wiring HTTP routes into a framework-specific app.\n+- `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order`: POST `/orders` behavior after route registration.\n+- `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order`: GET `/orders/<order_id>` behavior after route registration.\n+\n+## Data Flow\n+\n+### CLI startup\n+\n+1. `minisvc.cli:main` reads process environment.\n+2. `minisvc.config:load_settings` builds a `Settings` object.\n+3. `main` creates `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n+4. `OrderRepository.init_schema()` creates the `orders` table if it is missing.\n+5. The CLI prints `minisvc ready at ...` and exits.\n+\n+### HTTP create-order flow\n+\n+1. Some external application constructs a repository and calls `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo)`.\n+2. The registered POST callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order(payload, repo)`.\n+3. `create_order` extracts `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` from the payload and builds an `Order` dataclass.\n+4. `repo.save(order)` inserts the order into SQLite.\n+5. `order_event(order, \"created\")` generates a response event object.\n+6. The handler returns a dictionary response.\n+\n+### HTTP read flow\n+\n+1. The registered GET callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n+2. `repo.get(order_id)` reads a row from SQLite.\n+3. The handler returns either `{\"status\": \"missing\"}` or `{\"status\": \"ok\", \"order\": ..., \"event\": ...}`.\n+\n+## Storage\n+\n+- Storage engine: SQLite via Python `sqlite3`\n+- Path source: `MINISVC_DB`, defaulting to `orders.sqlite`\n+- Schema ownership: `OrderRepository.init_schema()`\n+- Tables actually created: only `orders`\n+- Audit persistence: none\n+\n+Each repository method opens a fresh SQLite connection with `sqlite3.connect(self.database_path)`. There is no connection pooling, no retry wrapper, and no migration/versioning layer.\n+\n+## Documentation vs Code Reality\n+\n+The README explicitly says the code is authoritative when docs disagree. In practice, the implementation is simpler than the design notes:\n+\n+- `MINISVC_READONLY=1` is parsed into `Settings.readonly`, but no write path checks it.\n+- `create_order` does not retry failed SQLite writes.\n+- Audit events are returned in response payloads only; there is no durable audit table.\n+\n+## Risks And Extension Points\n+\n+### Risks\n+\n+- Error handling is minimal. Missing payload keys, bad integer conversion, duplicate primary keys, or SQLite failures will raise exceptions directly from handlers.\n+- Configuration is only partly wired. `readonly` is loaded but ignored by the repository and handlers.\n+- Audit behavior is non-durable despite documentation claiming durable storage.\n+- The HTTP layer assumes an app object with `.post` and `.get`, but the repository contains no app factory or server bootstrap, so runtime integration is external and implicit.\n+\n+### Extension points\n+\n+- Enforce readonly mode in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` or inside `OrderRepository.save`.\n+- Add explicit request validation and translate failures into stable API responses.\n+- Introduce durable audit persistence in `minisvc/storage/repo.py` or a separate audit repository.\n+- Add an application bootstrap module that constructs the app and calls `register_routes` to make the HTTP runtime self-contained.\n","additions":86,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","relativePath":"workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\n+++ /workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\n@@ -0,0 +1,4 @@\n+claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n+\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads readonly into Settings; minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) unconditionally; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs insert with no readonly check\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may assume writes are prevented in readonly mode and accidentally modify production or maintenance databases.\"\n+\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 contains a single repo.save(order) call; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs one insert and has no retry loop or exception handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures will surface immediately and may produce unhandled 500-style failures instead of controlled retry behavior.\"\n+\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only builds a dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table; no module writes audit records\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may rely on an audit trail that does not exist, weakening compliance, debugging, and incident reconstruction.\"\n","additions":4,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv","relativePath":"workspace/out/risk_register.csv","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/risk_register.csv\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/risk_register.csv\n+++ /workspace/out/risk_register.csv\n@@ -0,0 +1,6 @@\n+risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\n+R1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 inserts directly into a local SQLite file; each method opens a new connection and there is no backup, migration, or retry layer\",\"Order data durability depends on a single local file and can be fragile in ephemeral or poorly managed runtime environments\",\"Define supported deployment storage, add backup/migration guidance, and consider a managed DB or explicit durability procedures\",\"Platform plus service owner\"\n+R2,audit behavior,\"README.md:8 claims durable audit storage, but minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an event dict and minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for created or read actions, limiting compliance evidence and post-incident analysis\",\"Either implement persisted audit records or remove/replace the claim and document the current ephemeral behavior\",\"Service owner\"\n+R3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY; minisvc/cli.py:8-11 uses database_path but no runtime code consults Settings.readonly\",\"Runtime behavior does not match configuration expectations, and defaulting to orders.sqlite may place data in an unintended working directory\",\"Enforce readonly mode in write paths and document or validate the database file location at startup\",\"Service owner\"\n+R4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 accesses payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(); no try/except or schema validation is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError and bubble up as unstable API failures\",\"Add request schema validation and convert validation failures into explicit client-facing error responses\",\"API owner\"\n+R5,HTTP integration contract,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes app.post and app.get methods, but the repo contains no app factory or framework dependency\",\"Integration can break silently if the host app contract differs, and new engineers have no in-repo runnable HTTP bootstrap\",\"Add a documented adapter contract or a concrete app bootstrap module with a smoke test\",\"Service owner\"\n","additions":6,"deletions":0},{"filePath":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","relativePath":"workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","type":"add","patch":"Index: /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md\n+++ /workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,50 @@\n+# minisvc Onboarding Plan\n+\n+## Read Order\n+\n+1. `README.md` to learn the intended behavior and note that code is authoritative.\n+2. `pyproject.toml` to find the packaged CLI entry point.\n+3. `minisvc/cli.py` for the simplest real runtime path.\n+4. `minisvc/config.py` and `minisvc/storage/repo.py` for configuration and persistence.\n+5. `minisvc/api/routes.py` and `minisvc/api/handlers.py` for request flow.\n+6. `minisvc/models.py` and `minisvc/audit.py` for shared data structures.\n+\n+Active runtime code is in the modules above. `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package markers, and `minisvc/__init__.py` is a minimal export file rather than business logic.\n+\n+## Local Run And Test Commands\n+\n+Run from the repository root:\n+\n+```bash\n+python -m minisvc.cli\n+MINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python -m minisvc.cli\n+python -m compileall minisvc\n+```\n+\n+There is no in-repo HTTP server bootstrap or automated test suite. For a quick handler smoke test:\n+\n+```bash\n+python - <<'PY'\n+from minisvc.api.handlers import create_order\n+from minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\n+\n+repo = OrderRepository('/tmp/minisvc-smoke.sqlite')\n+repo.init_schema()\n+print(create_order({'order_id': 'o-1', 'customer': 'Taylor', 'total_cents': '1234'}, repo))\n+PY\n+```\n+\n+## First Breakpoint Or Trace Point\n+\n+Start at `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order` on the `repo.save(order)` line.\n+\n+Why this spot:\n+\n+- It sits on the main write path.\n+- You can inspect payload parsing, `Order` construction, and the transition into SQLite persistence.\n+- It quickly reveals that readonly mode and retry behavior are not enforced.\n+\n+## Two Safe First Changes\n+\n+1. Add explicit request validation in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` so missing fields and bad `total_cents` values return stable errors instead of raw exceptions.\n+2. Wire `Settings.readonly` into the write path, either by checking it before `repo.save(order)` or by enforcing it in `OrderRepository.save`.\n","additions":50,"deletions":0}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nA workspace/out/module_map.json\nA workspace/out/architecture.md\nA workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv\nA workspace/out/risk_register.csv\nA workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","time":{"start":1788183061011,"end":1788183061023}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_03d5adaf75aabf8c016a9581b08dc087d2ad654ea6245b6a7d"}},"id":"prt_0580299da001XCJDZ1XsWnlkk0","sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","messageID":"msg_058026d47001wfhQJUXsYj3PCh"}}
