{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183068633,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_uLKTdC2CbHowkDhSqmGRuaew","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out</path>\n<type>directory</type>\n<entries>\narchitecture.md\ndoc_code_discrepancies.csv\nmodule_map.json\nonboarding_plan.md\nrisk_register.csv\n\n(5 entries)\n</entries>","metadata":{"preview":"architecture.md\ndoc_code_discrepancies.csv\nmodule_map.json\nonboarding_plan.md\nrisk_register.csv","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"directory","path":"/workspace/out","entries":["architecture.md","doc_code_discrepancies.csv","module_map.json","onboarding_plan.md","risk_register.csv"],"offset":1,"totalEntries":5,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out","time":{"start":1788183068617,"end":1788183068626}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_08aa87cbaf8f078b016a95821c550c87d291c860c3a22ec7d3"}},"id":"prt_058043fad0010YU4FvoIYGNIi1","sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","messageID":"msg_058042225001XYhGOMFKJyD4P5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183068652,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_uerZdoXpcDyfvfZ9ShawKAtp","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/architecture.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/architecture.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # minisvc Architecture Summary\n2: \n3: ## What This Service Actually Contains\n4: \n5: `minisvc` is a very small Python service skeleton with two real runtime surfaces:\n6: \n7: - A CLI bootstrap entry point at `minisvc.cli:main`\n8: - An HTTP route registration hook at `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n9: \n10: It persists orders to a local SQLite database through `OrderRepository`. The package marker files `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` do not contain business logic, and `minisvc/__init__.py` only exports names.\n11: \n12: ## Runtime Modules\n13: \n14: - `minisvc/cli.py`: startup path for the packaged `minisvc` command. Loads config, opens the repository, creates schema, prints readiness.\n15: - `minisvc/config.py`: defines `Settings` and `load_settings(env)`, reading `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY`.\n16: - `minisvc/models.py`: defines the `Order` dataclass.\n17: - `minisvc/audit.py`: builds an event dictionary for API responses. It does not write any audit records.\n18: - `minisvc/api/routes.py`: attaches HTTP handlers to an external app object via `app.post(...)` and `app.get(...)`.\n19: - `minisvc/api/handlers.py`: implements create and read order actions.\n20: - `minisvc/storage/repo.py`: owns SQLite schema creation and CRUD-like persistence for orders.\n21: \n22: ## Entry Points\n23: \n24: - `minisvc.cli:main`: declared in `pyproject.toml` as the `minisvc` console script.\n25: - `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`: integration point for wiring HTTP routes into a framework-specific app.\n26: - `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order`: POST `/orders` behavior after route registration.\n27: - `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order`: GET `/orders/<order_id>` behavior after route registration.\n28: \n29: ## Data Flow\n30: \n31: ### CLI startup\n32: \n33: 1. `minisvc.cli:main` reads process environment.\n34: 2. `minisvc.config:load_settings` builds a `Settings` object.\n35: 3. `main` creates `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n36: 4. `OrderRepository.init_schema()` creates the `orders` table if it is missing.\n37: 5. The CLI prints `minisvc ready at ...` and exits.\n38: \n39: ### HTTP create-order flow\n40: \n41: 1. Some external application constructs a repository and calls `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo)`.\n42: 2. The registered POST callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order(payload, repo)`.\n43: 3. `create_order` extracts `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` from the payload and builds an `Order` dataclass.\n44: 4. `repo.save(order)` inserts the order into SQLite.\n45: 5. `order_event(order, \"created\")` generates a response event object.\n46: 6. The handler returns a dictionary response.\n47: \n48: ### HTTP read flow\n49: \n50: 1. The registered GET callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n51: 2. `repo.get(order_id)` reads a row from SQLite.\n52: 3. The handler returns either `{\"status\": \"missing\"}` or `{\"status\": \"ok\", \"order\": ..., \"event\": ...}`.\n53: \n54: ## Storage\n55: \n56: - Storage engine: SQLite via Python `sqlite3`\n57: - Path source: `MINISVC_DB`, defaulting to `orders.sqlite`\n58: - Schema ownership: `OrderRepository.init_schema()`\n59: - Tables actually created: only `orders`\n60: - Audit persistence: none\n61: \n62: Each repository method opens a fresh SQLite connection with `sqlite3.connect(self.database_path)`. There is no connection pooling, no retry wrapper, and no migration/versioning layer.\n63: \n64: ## Documentation vs Code Reality\n65: \n66: The README explicitly says the code is authoritative when docs disagree. In practice, the implementation is simpler than the design notes:\n67: \n68: - `MINISVC_READONLY=1` is parsed into `Settings.readonly`, but no write path checks it.\n69: - `create_order` does not retry failed SQLite writes.\n70: - Audit events are returned in response payloads only; there is no durable audit table.\n71: \n72: ## Risks And Extension Points\n73: \n74: ### Risks\n75: \n76: - Error handling is minimal. Missing payload keys, bad integer conversion, duplicate primary keys, or SQLite failures will raise exceptions directly from handlers.\n77: - Configuration is only partly wired. `readonly` is loaded but ignored by the repository and handlers.\n78: - Audit behavior is non-durable despite documentation claiming durable storage.\n79: - The HTTP layer assumes an app object with `.post` and `.get`, but the repository contains no app factory or server bootstrap, so runtime integration is external and implicit.\n80: \n81: ### Extension points\n82: \n83: - Enforce readonly mode in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` or inside `OrderRepository.save`.\n84: - Add explicit request validation and translate failures into stable API responses.\n85: - Introduce durable audit persistence in `minisvc/storage/repo.py` or a separate audit repository.\n86: - Add an application bootstrap module that constructs the app and calls `register_routes` to make the HTTP runtime self-contained.\n\n(End of file - total 86 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# minisvc Architecture Summary\n\n## What This Service Actually Contains\n\n`minisvc` is a very small Python service skeleton with two real runtime surfaces:\n\n- A CLI bootstrap entry point at `minisvc.cli:main`\n- An HTTP route registration hook at `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n\nIt persists orders to a local SQLite database through `OrderRepository`. The package marker files `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` do not contain business logic, and `minisvc/__init__.py` only exports names.\n\n## Runtime Modules\n\n- `minisvc/cli.py`: startup path for the packaged `minisvc` command. Loads config, opens the repository, creates schema, prints readiness.\n- `minisvc/config.py`: defines `Settings` and `load_settings(env)`, reading `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY`.\n- `minisvc/models.py`: defines the `Order` dataclass.\n- `minisvc/audit.py`: builds an event dictionary for API responses. It does not write any audit records.\n- `minisvc/api/routes.py`: attaches HTTP handlers to an external app object via `app.post(...)` and `app.get(...)`.\n- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`: implements create and read order actions.\n- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`: owns SQLite schema creation and CRUD-like persistence for orders.","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/architecture.md","text":"# minisvc Architecture Summary\n\n## What This Service Actually Contains\n\n`minisvc` is a very small Python service skeleton with two real runtime surfaces:\n\n- A CLI bootstrap entry point at `minisvc.cli:main`\n- An HTTP route registration hook at `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`\n\nIt persists orders to a local SQLite database through `OrderRepository`. The package marker files `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` do not contain business logic, and `minisvc/__init__.py` only exports names.\n\n## Runtime Modules\n\n- `minisvc/cli.py`: startup path for the packaged `minisvc` command. Loads config, opens the repository, creates schema, prints readiness.\n- `minisvc/config.py`: defines `Settings` and `load_settings(env)`, reading `MINISVC_DB` and `MINISVC_READONLY`.\n- `minisvc/models.py`: defines the `Order` dataclass.\n- `minisvc/audit.py`: builds an event dictionary for API responses. It does not write any audit records.\n- `minisvc/api/routes.py`: attaches HTTP handlers to an external app object via `app.post(...)` and `app.get(...)`.\n- `minisvc/api/handlers.py`: implements create and read order actions.\n- `minisvc/storage/repo.py`: owns SQLite schema creation and CRUD-like persistence for orders.\n\n## Entry Points\n\n- `minisvc.cli:main`: declared in `pyproject.toml` as the `minisvc` console script.\n- `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes`: integration point for wiring HTTP routes into a framework-specific app.\n- `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order`: POST `/orders` behavior after route registration.\n- `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order`: GET `/orders/<order_id>` behavior after route registration.\n\n## Data Flow\n\n### CLI startup\n\n1. `minisvc.cli:main` reads process environment.\n2. `minisvc.config:load_settings` builds a `Settings` object.\n3. `main` creates `OrderRepository(settings.database_path)`.\n4. `OrderRepository.init_schema()` creates the `orders` table if it is missing.\n5. The CLI prints `minisvc ready at ...` and exits.\n\n### HTTP create-order flow\n\n1. Some external application constructs a repository and calls `minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo)`.\n2. The registered POST callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order(payload, repo)`.\n3. `create_order` extracts `order_id`, `customer`, and `total_cents` from the payload and builds an `Order` dataclass.\n4. `repo.save(order)` inserts the order into SQLite.\n5. `order_event(order, \"created\")` generates a response event object.\n6. The handler returns a dictionary response.\n\n### HTTP read flow\n\n1. The registered GET callback invokes `minisvc.api.handlers:get_order(order_id, repo)`.\n2. `repo.get(order_id)` reads a row from SQLite.\n3. The handler returns either `{\"status\": \"missing\"}` or `{\"status\": \"ok\", \"order\": ..., \"event\": ...}`.\n\n## Storage\n\n- Storage engine: SQLite via Python `sqlite3`\n- Path source: `MINISVC_DB`, defaulting to `orders.sqlite`\n- Schema ownership: `OrderRepository.init_schema()`\n- Tables actually created: only `orders`\n- Audit persistence: none\n\nEach repository method opens a fresh SQLite connection with `sqlite3.connect(self.database_path)`. There is no connection pooling, no retry wrapper, and no migration/versioning layer.\n\n## Documentation vs Code Reality\n\nThe README explicitly says the code is authoritative when docs disagree. In practice, the implementation is simpler than the design notes:\n\n- `MINISVC_READONLY=1` is parsed into `Settings.readonly`, but no write path checks it.\n- `create_order` does not retry failed SQLite writes.\n- Audit events are returned in response payloads only; there is no durable audit table.\n\n## Risks And Extension Points\n\n### Risks\n\n- Error handling is minimal. Missing payload keys, bad integer conversion, duplicate primary keys, or SQLite failures will raise exceptions directly from handlers.\n- Configuration is only partly wired. `readonly` is loaded but ignored by the repository and handlers.\n- Audit behavior is non-durable despite documentation claiming durable storage.\n- The HTTP layer assumes an app object with `.post` and `.get`, but the repository contains no app factory or server bootstrap, so runtime integration is external and implicit.\n\n### Extension points\n\n- Enforce readonly mode in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` or inside `OrderRepository.save`.\n- Add explicit request validation and translate failures into stable API responses.\n- Introduce durable audit persistence in `minisvc/storage/repo.py` or a separate audit repository.\n- Add an application bootstrap module that constructs the app and calls `register_routes` to make the HTTP runtime self-contained.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":86,"totalLines":86,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/architecture.md","time":{"start":1788183068620,"end":1788183068642}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_08aa87cbaf8f078b016a95821c551487d296007f5d0396380a"}},"id":"prt_058043fca0010cnHHHt6a8CnV0","sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","messageID":"msg_058042225001XYhGOMFKJyD4P5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183068652,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_UDdEiyzaSWOv8yeFbbqf5FsN","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/risk_register.csv</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\n2: R1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 inserts directly into a local SQLite file; each method opens a new connection and there is no backup, migration, or retry layer\",\"Order data durability depends on a single local file and can be fragile in ephemeral or poorly managed runtime environments\",\"Define supported deployment storage, add backup/migration guidance, and consider a managed DB or explicit durability procedures\",\"Platform plus service owner\"\n3: R2,audit behavior,\"README.md:8 claims durable audit storage, but minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an event dict and minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for created or read actions, limiting compliance evidence and post-incident analysis\",\"Either implement persisted audit records or remove/replace the claim and document the current ephemeral behavior\",\"Service owner\"\n4: R3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY; minisvc/cli.py:8-11 uses database_path but no runtime code consults Settings.readonly\",\"Runtime behavior does not match configuration expectations, and defaulting to orders.sqlite may place data in an unintended working directory\",\"Enforce readonly mode in write paths and document or validate the database file location at startup\",\"Service owner\"\n5: R4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 accesses payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(); no try/except or schema validation is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError and bubble up as unstable API failures\",\"Add request schema validation and convert validation failures into explicit client-facing error responses\",\"API owner\"\n6: R5,HTTP integration contract,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes app.post and app.get methods, but the repo contains no app factory or framework dependency\",\"Integration can break silently if the host app contract differs, and new engineers have no in-repo runnable HTTP bootstrap\",\"Add a documented adapter contract or a concrete app bootstrap module with a smoke test\",\"Service owner\"\n\n(End of file - total 6 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 inserts directly into a local SQLite file; each method opens a new connection and there is no backup, migration, or retry layer\",\"Order data durability depends on a single local file and can be fragile in ephemeral or poorly managed runtime environments\",\"Define supported deployment storage, add backup/migration guidance, and consider a managed DB or explicit durability procedures\",\"Platform plus service owner\"\nR2,audit behavior,\"README.md:8 claims durable audit storage, but minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an event dict and minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for created or read actions, limiting compliance evidence and post-incident analysis\",\"Either implement persisted audit records or remove/replace the claim and document the current ephemeral behavior\",\"Service owner\"\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY; minisvc/cli.py:8-11 uses database_path but no runtime code consults Settings.readonly\",\"Runtime behavior does not match configuration expectations, and defaulting to orders.sqlite may place data in an unintended working directory\",\"Enforce readonly mode in write paths and document or validate the database file location at startup\",\"Service owner\"\nR4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 accesses payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(); no try/except or schema validation is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError and bubble up as unstable API failures\",\"Add request schema validation and convert validation failures into explicit client-facing error responses\",\"API owner\"\nR5,HTTP integration contract,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes app.post and app.get methods, but the repo contains no app factory or framework dependency\",\"Integration can break silently if the host app contract differs, and new engineers have no in-repo runnable HTTP bootstrap\",\"Add a documented adapter contract or a concrete app bootstrap module with a smoke test\",\"Service owner\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/risk_register.csv","text":"risk_id,area,evidence,impact,mitigation,owner_hint\nR1,storage/data durability,\"minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 inserts directly into a local SQLite file; each method opens a new connection and there is no backup, migration, or retry layer\",\"Order data durability depends on a single local file and can be fragile in ephemeral or poorly managed runtime environments\",\"Define supported deployment storage, add backup/migration guidance, and consider a managed DB or explicit durability procedures\",\"Platform plus service owner\"\nR2,audit behavior,\"README.md:8 claims durable audit storage, but minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only returns an event dict and minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates no audit table\",\"No durable audit trail exists for created or read actions, limiting compliance evidence and post-incident analysis\",\"Either implement persisted audit records or remove/replace the claim and document the current ephemeral behavior\",\"Service owner\"\nR3,configuration/runtime environment,\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads MINISVC_DB and MINISVC_READONLY; minisvc/cli.py:8-11 uses database_path but no runtime code consults Settings.readonly\",\"Runtime behavior does not match configuration expectations, and defaulting to orders.sqlite may place data in an unintended working directory\",\"Enforce readonly mode in write paths and document or validate the database file location at startup\",\"Service owner\"\nR4,API input validation,\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:7-10 accesses payload keys directly and casts total_cents with int(); no try/except or schema validation is present\",\"Malformed requests can raise KeyError or ValueError and bubble up as unstable API failures\",\"Add request schema validation and convert validation failures into explicit client-facing error responses\",\"API owner\"\nR5,HTTP integration contract,\"minisvc/api/routes.py:4-6 assumes app.post and app.get methods, but the repo contains no app factory or framework dependency\",\"Integration can break silently if the host app contract differs, and new engineers have no in-repo runnable HTTP bootstrap\",\"Add a documented adapter contract or a concrete app bootstrap module with a smoke test\",\"Service owner\"","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":6,"totalLines":6,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/risk_register.csv","time":{"start":1788183068629,"end":1788183068644}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_08aa87cbaf8f078b016a95821c552087d2b8885b2016a1a98c"}},"id":"prt_058043fd0001J029i9WAV0TnZt","sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","messageID":"msg_058042225001XYhGOMFKJyD4P5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183068652,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_7iLIr5Urj6gpWhkyZolRX1Y4","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n2: \"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads readonly into Settings; minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) unconditionally; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs insert with no readonly check\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may assume writes are prevented in readonly mode and accidentally modify production or maintenance databases.\"\n3: \"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 contains a single repo.save(order) call; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs one insert and has no retry loop or exception handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures will surface immediately and may produce unhandled 500-style failures instead of controlled retry behavior.\"\n4: \"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only builds a dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table; no module writes audit records\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may rely on an audit trail that does not exist, weakening compliance, debugging, and incident reconstruction.\"\n\n(End of file - total 4 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads readonly into Settings; minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) unconditionally; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs insert with no readonly check\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may assume writes are prevented in readonly mode and accidentally modify production or maintenance databases.\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 contains a single repo.save(order) call; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs one insert and has no retry loop or exception handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures will surface immediately and may produce unhandled 500-style failures instead of controlled retry behavior.\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only builds a dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table; no module writes audit records\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may rely on an audit trail that does not exist, weakening compliance, debugging, and incident reconstruction.\"","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","text":"claim,doc_source,code_evidence,assessment,risk\n\"MINISVC_READONLY=1 blocks all write paths\",\"README.md:6\",\"minisvc/config.py:10-14 loads readonly into Settings; minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 calls repo.save(order) unconditionally; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs insert with no readonly check\",\"contradicted\",\"Operators may assume writes are prevented in readonly mode and accidentally modify production or maintenance databases.\"\n\"create_order retries failed SQLite writes twice before returning an error response\",\"README.md:7\",\"minisvc/api/handlers.py:6-13 contains a single repo.save(order) call; minisvc/storage/repo.py:17-22 performs one insert and has no retry loop or exception handling\",\"contradicted\",\"Transient database failures will surface immediately and may produce unhandled 500-style failures instead of controlled retry behavior.\"\n\"Audit events are stored in a durable audit table\",\"README.md:8\",\"minisvc/audit.py:4-10 only builds a dict; minisvc/storage/repo.py:11-15 creates only the orders table; no module writes audit records\",\"contradicted\",\"Teams may rely on an audit trail that does not exist, weakening compliance, debugging, and incident reconstruction.\"","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":4,"totalLines":4,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/doc_code_discrepancies.csv","time":{"start":1788183068623,"end":1788183068645}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_08aa87cbaf8f078b016a95821c551887d29c1a8e005ecbab94"}},"id":"prt_058043fcd001EYcP8zYGrsMlRn","sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","messageID":"msg_058042225001XYhGOMFKJyD4P5"}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788183068652,"sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"read","callID":"call_UQ985W4kedzHLzU9IMl6QHxP","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"filePath":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md"},"output":"<path>/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md</path>\n<type>file</type>\n<content>\n1: # minisvc Onboarding Plan\n2: \n3: ## Read Order\n4: \n5: 1. `README.md` to learn the intended behavior and note that code is authoritative.\n6: 2. `pyproject.toml` to find the packaged CLI entry point.\n7: 3. `minisvc/cli.py` for the simplest real runtime path.\n8: 4. `minisvc/config.py` and `minisvc/storage/repo.py` for configuration and persistence.\n9: 5. `minisvc/api/routes.py` and `minisvc/api/handlers.py` for request flow.\n10: 6. `minisvc/models.py` and `minisvc/audit.py` for shared data structures.\n11: \n12: Active runtime code is in the modules above. `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package markers, and `minisvc/__init__.py` is a minimal export file rather than business logic.\n13: \n14: ## Local Run And Test Commands\n15: \n16: Run from the repository root:\n17: \n18: ```bash\n19: python -m minisvc.cli\n20: MINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python -m minisvc.cli\n21: python -m compileall minisvc\n22: ```\n23: \n24: There is no in-repo HTTP server bootstrap or automated test suite. For a quick handler smoke test:\n25: \n26: ```bash\n27: python - <<'PY'\n28: from minisvc.api.handlers import create_order\n29: from minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\n30: \n31: repo = OrderRepository('/tmp/minisvc-smoke.sqlite')\n32: repo.init_schema()\n33: print(create_order({'order_id': 'o-1', 'customer': 'Taylor', 'total_cents': '1234'}, repo))\n34: PY\n35: ```\n36: \n37: ## First Breakpoint Or Trace Point\n38: \n39: Start at `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order` on the `repo.save(order)` line.\n40: \n41: Why this spot:\n42: \n43: - It sits on the main write path.\n44: - You can inspect payload parsing, `Order` construction, and the transition into SQLite persistence.\n45: - It quickly reveals that readonly mode and retry behavior are not enforced.\n46: \n47: ## Two Safe First Changes\n48: \n49: 1. Add explicit request validation in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` so missing fields and bad `total_cents` values return stable errors instead of raw exceptions.\n50: 2. Wire `Settings.readonly` into the write path, either by checking it before `repo.save(order)` or by enforcing it in `OrderRepository.save`.\n\n(End of file - total 50 lines)\n</content>","metadata":{"preview":"# minisvc Onboarding Plan\n\n## Read Order\n\n1. `README.md` to learn the intended behavior and note that code is authoritative.\n2. `pyproject.toml` to find the packaged CLI entry point.\n3. `minisvc/cli.py` for the simplest real runtime path.\n4. `minisvc/config.py` and `minisvc/storage/repo.py` for configuration and persistence.\n5. `minisvc/api/routes.py` and `minisvc/api/handlers.py` for request flow.\n6. `minisvc/models.py` and `minisvc/audit.py` for shared data structures.\n\nActive runtime code is in the modules above. `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package markers, and `minisvc/__init__.py` is a minimal export file rather than business logic.\n\n## Local Run And Test Commands\n\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```bash\npython -m minisvc.cli\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python -m minisvc.cli","truncated":false,"loaded":[],"display":{"type":"file","path":"/workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","text":"# minisvc Onboarding Plan\n\n## Read Order\n\n1. `README.md` to learn the intended behavior and note that code is authoritative.\n2. `pyproject.toml` to find the packaged CLI entry point.\n3. `minisvc/cli.py` for the simplest real runtime path.\n4. `minisvc/config.py` and `minisvc/storage/repo.py` for configuration and persistence.\n5. `minisvc/api/routes.py` and `minisvc/api/handlers.py` for request flow.\n6. `minisvc/models.py` and `minisvc/audit.py` for shared data structures.\n\nActive runtime code is in the modules above. `minisvc/api/__init__.py` and `minisvc/storage/__init__.py` are package markers, and `minisvc/__init__.py` is a minimal export file rather than business logic.\n\n## Local Run And Test Commands\n\nRun from the repository root:\n\n```bash\npython -m minisvc.cli\nMINISVC_DB=/tmp/minisvc.sqlite python -m minisvc.cli\npython -m compileall minisvc\n```\n\nThere is no in-repo HTTP server bootstrap or automated test suite. For a quick handler smoke test:\n\n```bash\npython - <<'PY'\nfrom minisvc.api.handlers import create_order\nfrom minisvc.storage.repo import OrderRepository\n\nrepo = OrderRepository('/tmp/minisvc-smoke.sqlite')\nrepo.init_schema()\nprint(create_order({'order_id': 'o-1', 'customer': 'Taylor', 'total_cents': '1234'}, repo))\nPY\n```\n\n## First Breakpoint Or Trace Point\n\nStart at `minisvc/api/handlers.py:create_order` on the `repo.save(order)` line.\n\nWhy this spot:\n\n- It sits on the main write path.\n- You can inspect payload parsing, `Order` construction, and the transition into SQLite persistence.\n- It quickly reveals that readonly mode and retry behavior are not enforced.\n\n## Two Safe First Changes\n\n1. Add explicit request validation in `minisvc.api.handlers:create_order` so missing fields and bad `total_cents` values return stable errors instead of raw exceptions.\n2. Wire `Settings.readonly` into the write path, either by checking it before `repo.save(order)` or by enforcing it in `OrderRepository.save`.","lineStart":1,"lineEnd":50,"totalLines":50,"truncated":false}},"title":"workspace/out/onboarding_plan.md","time":{"start":1788183068631,"end":1788183068646}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_08aa87cbaf8f078b016a95821c552487d29dbbda7ef4a06760"}},"id":"prt_058043fd6001gj6yR316MhCpAj","sessionID":"ses_fa7fe42cbffeFQ7HIc8Ial1VtO","messageID":"msg_058042225001XYhGOMFKJyD4P5"}}
