onse with an audit-style event payload.\",\n            \"notable_details\": [\n                \"Requires payload keys order_id, customer, and total_cents.\",\n                \"Casts total_cents with int().\",\n                \"Does not catch validation or database exceptions.\",\n                \"Does not retry failed writes or consult readonly settings.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"identifier\": \"minisvc.api.handlers:get_order\",\n            \"summary\": \"Fetches an order by id and returns either a missing response or the order contents plus an audit-style read event.\",\n            \"notable_details\": [\n                \"Returns order.__dict__ directly for successful reads.\",\n                \"No explicit input validation beyond repository query parameterization.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"identifier\": \"minisvc.audit:order_event\",\n            \"summary\": \"Constructs a dictionary describing an order action for API responses.\",\n            \"notable_details\": [\n                \"Pure function with no storage or external side effects.\",\n                \"Supports both created and read actions based on caller input.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.init_schema\",\n            \"summary\": \"Ensures the orders table exists in SQLite.\",\n            \"notable_details\": [\n                \"Only creates the orders table; there is no audit table.\",\n                \"Relies on sqlite3 context manager transaction behavior.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.save\",\n            \"summary\": \"Inserts an Order into the orders table.\",\n            \"notable_details\": [\n                \"Opens a new SQLite connection per call.\",\n                \"No retry loop, upsert behavior, or error handling.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"identifier\": \"minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository.get\",\n            \"summary\": \"Looks up an order row by primary key and reconstructs an Order object if found.\",\n            \"notable_details\": [\n                \"Uses a parameterized query for order_id.\",\n                \"Returns None when no row exists.\"\n            ]\n        }\n    ],\n    \"runtime_flows\": [\n        {\n            \"name\": \"CLI startup flow\",\n            \"steps\": [\n                \"The packaging script entry point invokes minisvc.cli:main.\",\n                \"main reads process environment and calls minisvc.config:load_settings.\",\n                \"load_settings builds Settings with database_path and readonly fields.\",\n                \"main instantiates minisvc.storage.repo:OrderRepository using settings.database_path.\",\n                \"main calls OrderRepository.init_schema, which creates the SQLite orders table if needed.\",\n                \"main prints a readiness message containing the database path and exits with status code 0.\"\n            ]\n        },\n        {\n            \"name\": \"HTTP create-order flow\",\n            \"steps\": [\n                \"An external web app calls minisvc.api.routes:register_routes(app, repo).\",\n                \"register_routes binds POST /orders to a lambda that forwards payload and repo into minisvc.api.handlers:create_order.\",\n                \"create_order reads payload['order_id'], payload['customer'], and payload['total_cents'] and constructs minisvc.models:Order.\",\n                \"create_order calls OrderRepository.save, which inserts the record into the SQLite orders table.\",\n                \"create_order calls minisvc.audit:order_event with action='created'.\",\n                \"create_order returns a response dict containing status, order_id, and the generated event payload.\",\n                \"If payload fields are missing or SQLite insert fails, the exception propagates because